{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The first interpretation</b><br>אחזו. (A form of) command, and its pattern is like שחדו (give), and it has a third [parallel] occurrence in Scripture: אהבו את י״י (love HaShem)." "מחבלים. Destroyers, like וחבל את מעשה ידיך (and destroy the work of Your hands)." "<b>The second interpretation</b><br>[She answered and] said to her maidens: Go to the vineyard and guard it from the foxes, for my beloved is mine and I am his, who is like dust pasturing among lilies whose fragrance wafts." "<b>The third interpretation</b><br>אחזו לנו שועלים. These are the worshippers of the calf."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:06.807086518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}